---------------------------------------------------------------------------
Third-party components

1) LiteRT (Google LLC)
   Maven: com.google.ai.edge.litert
   License: Apache License 2.0
   Used for on-device multilingual-e5-small text embeddings.

2) LiteRT-LM (Google LLC)
   Maven: com.google.ai.edge.litertlm:litertlm-android:0.15.0
   Source: https://github.com/google-ai-edge/LiteRT-LM
   License: Apache License 2.0
   Used for on-device LLM orchestration (Gemma `.litertlm`).

3) Gemma model weights (Google)
   Not included in this repository. Users obtain `.litertlm` weights separately
   (SAF import or model-prep download from hf-mirror) and keep them on device.
   Terms: https://ai.google.dev/gemma/terms
   Docs: https://ai.google.dev/gemma

4) multilingual-e5-small (intfloat)
   Source: https://huggingface.co/intfloat/multilingual-e5-small
   License: MIT
   The release application redistributes a locally converted TFLite artifact and
   its tokenizer under assets/embedding/ (prepared by
   android/scripts/prepare-embedding-model.sh; weight binaries are gitignored).
   Used only for on-device document and query embeddings; the application never
   downloads this model at runtime.

5) PdfBox-Android (Apache PdfBox / Tom Roush)
   Maven: com.tom-roush:pdfbox-android
   License: Apache License 2.0
   Used for PDF text-layer extraction on device.

6) ML Kit Text Recognition Chinese (Google)
   Used for OCR on sparse/scanned PDF pages. Subject to Google ML Kit terms;
   not redistributed as source in this repository.

7) OkHttp (Square)
   License: Apache License 2.0
   Used only by the model-prep download path (hf-mirror). Knowledge-base
   import / index / retrieve / generate do not use the network.

8) Kotlin / AndroidX / Jetpack Compose / kotlinx.coroutines
   License: Apache License 2.0

9) Material Icon Theme file icons (Material Extensions)
   Source: https://github.com/material-extensions/vscode-material-icon-theme
   License: MIT
   Bundled PNG derivatives (Word / Excel / PowerPoint / PDF / Markdown /
   plain text) under res/drawable-*/file_icon_*.png for the knowledge-base
   document list.
